  <!-- 6. The celebrations: accordion of image panels (one open on desktop; stacked, collapsible cards on phones).
       Each trigger controls its body (aria-controls / id). Aghd and Nikah are described distinctly. -->
  <section class="section" id="celebrations" aria-labelledby="celebrations-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__head">
        <h2 id="celebrations-title" class="reveal">The celebrations</h2>
        <svg class="scribble kashida-draw" viewBox="0 0 320 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12 C 90 12, 150 19, 212 13 S 300 9, 316 12"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="accordion reveal" data-accordion>
        <article class="accordion__panel is-open">
          <div class="accordion__media"><img src="assets/img/pom-open-closeup.jpg" width="2000" height="1123" alt="An opened pomegranate, seeds packed tight" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
          <button class="accordion__trigger" type="button" aria-controls="celebration-1" aria-expanded="true"><span class="visually-hidden">Show Sofreh Aghd</span></button>
          <span class="accordion__label" aria-hidden="true">Sofreh Aghd</span>
          <div class="accordion__body" id="celebration-1">
            <p class="fa" lang="fa" dir="rtl">سفرهٔ عقد</p>
            <h3>Sofreh Aghd</h3>
            <p class="accordion__desc">The Persian ceremony at the spread: the mirror, the candlesticks, the sugar cones ground over the cloth held above the couple. We brief your sofreh designer and check the spread against the sofreh key before the elders are seated.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="accordion__panel">
          <div class="accordion__media"><img src="assets/img/pom-pile.jpg" width="1411" height="2000" alt="A pile of pomegranates" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
          <button class="accordion__trigger" type="button" aria-controls="celebration-2" aria-expanded="false"><span class="visually-hidden">Show Nikah</span></button>
          <span class="accordion__label" aria-hidden="true">Nikah</span>
          <div class="accordion__body" id="celebration-2">
            <p class="fa" lang="fa" dir="rtl">نکاح</p>
            <h3>Nikah</h3>
            <p class="accordion__desc">The Islamic marriage contract, read before witnesses and both families. Quiet, exact, unhurried. If your family observes the aina mosaf, as many Afghan families do, it has its own moment: the mirror, the Quran, the elders close.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="accordion__panel">
          <div class="accordion__media"><img src="assets/img/pom-in-hand.jpg" width="1500" height="2000" alt="A pomegranate held in an open hand" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
          <button class="accordion__trigger" type="button" aria-controls="celebration-3" aria-expanded="false"><span class="visually-hidden">Show Mehndi and Sangeet</span></button>
          <span class="accordion__label" aria-hidden="true">Mehndi &amp; Sangeet</span>
          <div class="accordion__body" id="celebration-3">
            <p class="fa" lang="fa" dir="rtl">حنابندان · مهندی</p>
            <h3>Mehndi &amp; Sangeet</h3>
            <p class="accordion__desc">Henna, blessings, music and dancing, across the gatherings your family chooses: hana-bandan for Persian families, khina for Afghan families, mehndi and the sangeet for South Asian families. We run each as your family keeps it.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="accordion__panel">
          <div class="accordion__media"><img src="assets/img/pom-tree-night.jpg" width="1125" height="2000" alt="A pomegranate tree at night" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
          <button class="accordion__trigger" type="button" aria-controls="celebration-4" aria-expanded="false"><span class="visually-hidden">Show Haldi and Pheras</span></button>
          <span class="accordion__label" aria-hidden="true">Haldi &amp; Pheras</span>
          <div class="accordion__body" id="celebration-4">
            <p class="eyebrow">Hindu ceremonies</p>
            <h3>Haldi &amp; Pheras</h3>
            <p class="accordion__desc">The pheras under the mandap, with the pandit, at the muhurat your family's priest has set: your ceremony, in the sequence agreed with your officiant. If your family observes the haldi, the turmeric before the wedding.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="accordion__panel">
          <div class="accordion__media"><img src="assets/img/pom-pile.jpg" width="1411" height="2000" alt="A pile of pomegranates" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
          <button class="accordion__trigger" type="button" aria-controls="celebration-5" aria-expanded="false"><span class="visually-hidden">Show Anand Karaj</span></button>
          <span class="accordion__label" aria-hidden="true">Anand Karaj</span>
          <div class="accordion__body" id="celebration-5">
            <p class="eyebrow">Sikh ceremony</p>
            <h3>Anand Karaj</h3>
            <p class="accordion__desc">The Sikh ceremony before the Guru Granth Sahib: the four laavan as the hymns are sung, in the sequence agreed with your family and the granthi. We coordinate timing with the gurdwara.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="accordion__panel">
          <div class="accordion__media"><img src="assets/img/pom-open-closeup.jpg" width="2000" height="1123" alt="An opened pomegranate, seeds packed tight" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
          <button class="accordion__trigger" type="button" aria-controls="celebration-6" aria-expanded="false"><span class="visually-hidden">Show Reception and Walima</span></button>
          <span class="accordion__label" aria-hidden="true">Reception &amp; Walima</span>
          <div class="accordion__body" id="celebration-6">
            <p class="fa" lang="fa" dir="rtl">جشن عروسی · ولیمه</p>
            <h3>Reception &amp; Walima</h3>
            <p class="accordion__desc">The walima, the groom's family's feast after the nikah, and the reception, on one night or two as your family keeps it. One timeline, called with the venue and every vendor, from the elders' blessing to the last dance.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p style="text-align:center;margin-top:32px" class="reveal"><a class="link-arrow" href="weddings.html">Every tradition, in its own words</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

